<title>SWITZERLAND: BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BOBSLEIGH-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ST. MORITZ, Switzerland 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of the</p>
<p>bobsleigh world championship two-man competition on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Switzerland I (Reto Goetschi/Guido Acklin) four minutes,</p>
<p>17.59 seconds (first run 1:04.55/second run 1:04.55/third run/</p>
<p>1:04.04/fourth run 1:04.45)</p>
<p>2. Italy I (Guenther Huber/Antonio Tartaglia) 4:18.57 (1:04.54/</p>
<p>1:04.89/1:04.40/1:04.74)</p>
<p>3. U.S. I (Brian Shimer/Robert Olesen) 4:18.67 (1:04.74/1:04.75</p>
<p>/1:04.41/1:04.77)</p>
<p>4. Canada I (Pierre Lueders/Dave MacEachern) 4:18.73 (1:04.73/</p>
<p>1:04.91/1:04.64/1:04.45)  5. Germany I (Sepp Dostthaler/Thomas</p>
<p>Platzer) 4:19.07 (1:04.58/ 1:04.95/1:04.70/1:04.84)</p>
<p>6. Canada II (Chris Lori/Sheridan Baptiste) 4:19.09 (1:04.71/</p>
<p>1:04.97/1:04.60/1:04.81)</p>
<p>7. Latvia I (Sandis Prusis/Adris Pluksna) 4:19.55 (1:04.87/</p>
<p>1:05.15/1:04.60/1:04.93)</p>
<p>8. Britain I (Sean Olsson/Dean Ward) 4:20.15 (1:05.10/1:05.26/</p>
<p>1:04.56/1:05.23)  9. Germany II (Matthias Benesch/Lars Bolte)</p>
<p>4:20.20 (1:05.03/ 1:05.18/1:04.94/1:05.05)</p>
<p>10. U.S. II (Jim Herberich/Garrettt Hines) 4:20.31 (1:05.23/</p>
<p>1:05.06/1:04.63/1:06.39)</p>
